To certify each commit use:

    git commit -s -m "Short description"

This adds a Signed-off-by: Name <email> line to the commit. Contributors
must use their own identity and an address they have chosen to include
in the public Git history (including a GitHub-provided no-reply address
where suitable). DCO sign-off is a provenance certification; it is not
a transfer of copyright to the project or the association.
